<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Detailed Results of the Scalability Analysis</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Section <a href="#S4.SS5" title="4.5 Scalability Analysis ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Beyond Higher Rank: Token-wise Input-Output Projections for Efficient Low-Rank Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a>, the scalability of TopLoRA was evaluated using LLama-3-8B on mathematical reasoning tasks from two perspectives: the LoRA rank and tuning granularity. Figure <a href="#S4.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 4.5 Scalability Analysis ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Beyond Higher Rank: Token-wise Input-Output Projections for Efficient Low-Rank Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> presents the average accuracy of different settings across sub-tasks. Complete experimental results are available in Tables <a href="#A2.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ B.2 Detailed Results of the Scalability Analysis ‣ Appendix B Additional Experimental Results ‣ Beyond Higher Rank: Token-wise Input-Output Projections for Efficient Low-Rank Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> and <a href="#A2.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ B.2 Detailed Results of the Scalability Analysis ‣ Appendix B Additional Experimental Results ‣ Beyond Higher Rank: Token-wise Input-Output Projections for Efficient Low-Rank Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> for further comparison.</p>
</div>
